From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: disable interrupts during firmware crash recovery

ath11k_core_reconfigure_on_crash() tears the data path down while the
host interrupts and copy-engine interrupts are still live, so a CE or
DP interrupt can land in structures the same function is freeing. On
IPQ8074 with NSS offload this is reachable on every firmware fatal.

The reset path already disables them - ath11k_core_reset() does so
before scheduling the reconfigure - so the crash path is the only one
that arrives here with interrupts enabled. Gate on ab->is_reset and
disable both interrupt classes there.

This is the change submitted upstream as "wifi: ath11k: disable
interrupts during firmware crash recovery"; it is carried here because
the NSS tree reaches this path on hardware where it is not optional.

It depends on the CRASH_FLUSH guard in 999-927: without it,
ath11k_hif_ce_irq_disable() on the crash path would write the CE
interrupt-enable registers of a Q6 that TrustZone is tearing down,
which is the synchronous external abort 999-927 exists to prevent.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
index ba04535..48f14dd 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
@@ -2427,6 +2427,16 @@ static int ath11k_core_reconfigure_on_crash(struct ath11k_base *ab)
 	ab->nss.enabled = false;
 
 	ath11k_thermal_unregister(ab);
+
+	/*
+	 * ath11k_core_reset() already disabled the interrupts on the reset
+	 * path; only the firmware crash path reaches here with them live.
+	 */
+	if (!ab->is_reset) {
+		ath11k_hif_irq_disable(ab);
+		ath11k_hif_ce_irq_disable(ab);
+	}
+
 	ath11k_dp_pdev_free(ab);
 	ath11k_cfr_deinit(ab);
 	ath11k_spectral_deinit(ab);
